<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  robot: kmjh_mp18_arm_kg1_v4. Canonical source: this directly authored XML.
  consumers: CAD Viewer/RViz; future Isaac import requires separate validation.
  Units: m, kg, s, rad. Right-handed Base/world +Z up, CAD mm scaled once to m.
  Sources: current MP18 manipulator-v2 working CAD, MP16 drive, MP10 wrist,
  MP6 reducer and KG1. Source hashes and preserved originals: provenance.json.
  Scaffolding: src/simulation/urdf_mp18_v4/assets.py computes meshes/numbers only;
  verify.py independently checks this XML. Neither is an XML generator.
  Joint ledger: J1 Base>Link1 +Z; J2 Link1>Link2 +Y; J3 Link2>Link3 +Y;
  J4 Link3>Link4 +X; J5 Link4>Link5 +Y; J6 Link5>Link6 +X.
  Positive arm rotation follows right hand about these child/joint axes.
  Origin translations in parent frames: z .096, z .078, x .165, x .165,
  x .078, x .140. Source: MP18 layout.offsets; J3 module rotated 90deg in CAD.
  URDF arm zero is CAD display [15,-50,70,15,25,-10]deg, not physical zero.
  CAD absolute angle = URDF relative angle + display offset; joint origin RPY
  embeds each display angle once. Physical link frames coincide with joints.
  Base is a physical root at CAD world. Links1..6 inherit joint frames above.
  Mesh local = inverse(T_link(CAD0))*Fr*source; world = T_link(display)*local.
  Every visual/collision mesh is in owning link coordinates, metres, scale1,
  identity origin. Multiple colour visual meshes intentionally partition each
  canonical meshes/NAME.stl; numeric-ledger.json lists membership and bounds.
  Each collision file concatenates per-part convex hull shells, not one global
  convex hull. Annular bores/guide holes close; false contacts are possible.
  Dynamic mesh decomposition, contact and self-collision acceptance NOT_RUN.
  KG1_mount is fixed at Link6 x .028m; G axes +X=Link6+Y,+Y=Link6+Z,+Z=Link6+X.
  KG1 is fixed group F; KG1_A/B are jaws/pads/screws with G-parallel frames;
  KG1_R is pinion/spline/horn/screws, pivot G z .026m, +Y rotation.
  Gripper assets are CAD closed u0/FLAT, R centred at pivot. Joint origins put
  jaws at +/-20mm and rotor at -20/13.5rad exactly once for default 40mm gap.
  opening_m is full gap0..94mm, expressed in m: d=opening_m/2-.020;
  A=d, B=d, R=-d/.0135.
  Positive A moves G-X, B moves G+X; R is right hand about G+Y.
  B mimics A*1; R mimics A*(-74.07407407407408). 9 movable/7 independent DOF.
  tool0 is frame-only, G z .103m, J6 x .131m; nominal uncalibrated grasp point.
  Inertial ledger: all 11 physical links use numeric-ledger.json computed mass,
  local COM, full COM tensor in link axes (inertial rpy0). Printed parts use
  slicer masses and uniform mesh-volume inertia, not solid-density mass.
  Purchased items use original estimated box/point models. 117 point-I0 items
  contribute no intrinsic inertia; their parallel-axis contribution is kept.
  All masses/COM/tensors are estimates, not weighed/calibrated robot properties.
  MP18 original173 masses rebuilt; KG1 lump .1842kg removed once and split into
  47 actual components. 219 mass entries, total8.863854736164349kg conserved.
  KG1 allocation assumptions: servo54.8g F/spline.2g R; horn3g R; rods13.19g F;
  screws9g split F/A/B/R16:4:4:9 of33; within category volume allocation.
  Whole CAD0 closed COM changes [-7.849,+7.376,-16.857]um from lump refinement.
  Explicit mismatch: 6818 bearing mass belongs Link1 in original load model,
  visual belongs Base; preserved approximation, not resolved bearing dynamics.
  Motors shown as central reference envelopes; driver point masses retained.
  Clearance/connector/slot-end envelopes excluded from duplicated visuals.
  Limits: designer CAD absolute proposals J1[-170,170],J2[-100,0],J3[-20,120],
  J4[-120,120],J5[-90,90],J6[-170,170]deg, shifted by display offsets below.
  These lie within independent-axis C5 samples, not safe physical limits or a
  collision-free combined configuration space. J2/J3/J5 samples can cross desk.
  Effort/velocity/damping/friction unchanged from v3 starter simulation caps:
  arm3/6/5/2/2/1Nm,.5rad/s,.05/0; jaws10N,.02m/s; pinion.2Nm,2rad/s.
  They are not motor/reducer ratings and have not been accepted for new mass.
  57D terminal placement remains a 42D-derived assumption in source CAD.
  UNKNOWN: physical zeros, encoder/motor signs, measured ratios and hardware IDs.
  NOT_RUN: Isaac/USD import, gravity/stop/motion, continuous contact, hardware.
  Older simulation outcomes do not validate this changed model. No hardware I/O.
-->
